  "bodyTypst": "A population is modeled by a function $P$ that satisfies the logistic differential equation $ frac(d P,d t)= frac(P,5)lr((1 - frac(P,12))) . $\n\n(a) If $P(0)= 3$, what is $lim_(t -> oo) P(t)$ ?\n\nIf $P(0)= 20$, what is $lim_(t -> oo) P(t)$ ?\n\n(b) If $P(0)= 3$, for what value of $P$ is the population growing the fastest?\n\n(c) A different population is modeled by a function $Y$ that satisfies the separable differential equation\n\n$ frac(d Y,d t)= frac(Y,5)lr((1 - frac(t,12))) $\n\nFind $Y(t)$ if $Y(0)= 3$.\n\n(d) For the function $Y$ found in part (c), what is $lim_(t -> oo) Y(t)$ ?",
